## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/h24/fr.png" alt="France" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', marginRight: '8px'}} />France

France is navigating multiple simultaneous transformations while adopting a more confrontational stance toward US pressure under Trump's second presidency. The country faces continued domestic political fragmentation with governance dependent on constitutional workarounds, while the 2027 electoral dynamics crystallize around Le Pen's appeal verdict. Internationally, France positions itself as leader of European resistance to American coercion through public criticism, new diplomatic communication strategies, and support for trade retaliation, while maintaining alliance frameworks. The central tension remains between France's institutional leadership ambitions and the gravitational pull of fiscal constraints, political instability, and an increasingly polarized domestic political environment heading into the decisive 2027 election cycle.

**Key developments:**

- **Diplomatic:** President Macron delivered combative speech at World Economic Forum criticizing US trade policies while wearing sunglasses due to eye condition. Called out attempts to subordinate Europe, drawing mockery from Trump but boosting French eyewear manufacturer stock 28%. *([Multiple outlets](https://www.bfmtv.com, https://lemonde.fr, https://lefigaro.fr), 2026-01-20)*
- **Diplomatic:** Trump threatened 200% tariffs on European countries opposing his Greenland plans and leaked Macron's private messages. Later announced NATO framework and suspended tariff threats after talks with Secretary General Rutte. Danish PM firmly rejected NATO's authority to negotiate territorial sovereignty. *([Le Figaro](https://lefigaro.fr/international/groenland-pourquoi-la-souverainete-de-l-ile-n-est-pas-negociable-et-surtout-pas-par-l-otan-20260123), 2026-01-19)*
- **Diplomatic:** Foreign Ministry launched new X account using memes, irony and pop culture to counter disinformation and attacks from Russia and US. Gained 80,000 followers, representing major shift from traditional diplomatic communication toward confrontational digital engagement. *([Challenges](https://www.challenges.fr/economie/nous-changeons-de-posturenous-lassumons-le-quai-dorsay-repond-a-nos-questions-sur-la-strategie-french-response_637685), 2026-01-19)*
- **Diplomatic:** CNCDH Secretary General Magali Lafourcade revealed US State Department officials approached her in May 2025 seeking to portray Le Pen's conviction as political persecution. She reported the contact to the Foreign Ministry as potential interference in French judicial proceedings. *([Le Parisien](https://leparisien.fr/politique/condamnation-de-marine-le-pen-une-magistrate-affirme-avoir-ete-approchee-par-des-emissaires-de-washington-avec-une-visee-dingerence-20-01-2026-IDNIH6WT65CUVF7PKIXHEOSSEU.php), 2026-01-20)*
- **Domestic:** PM Lecornu broke his promise and used Article 49.3 to pass 2026 budget after parliamentary negotiations stalled. Survived two censure motions from LFI and RN, then announced plan to build 2 million homes by 2030. Demonstrates continued minority government dependence on constitutional workarounds. *([Multiple outlets](https://lemonde.fr, https://20minutes.fr, https://bfmtv.com), 2026-01-20)*
- **Unexpected:** French magistrate reveals US interference attempt in Le Pen judicial case.

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Macron confronts Trump at Davos wearing viral sunglasses, criticizes US attempts to 'subordinate Europe'** — President Macron delivered a combative speech at Davos criticizing US trade policies while wearing aviator sunglasses due to an eye condition. The sunglasses went viral globally, boosting the French manufacturer's stock by 28% and drawing mockery from Trump. *([bfmtv.com](https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/01/20/macron-denounces-us-competition-aiming-to-subordinate-europe_6749617_4.html))*
- **Trump threatens Greenland annexation and European tariffs, then announces NATO accord framework** — Trump threatened to impose 200% tariffs on European countries opposing his Greenland acquisition plans and leaked private messages from Macron. He later announced a NATO accord framework and suspended tariff threats after talks with Secretary General Mark Rutte. *([lemonde.fr](https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/01/21/trump-annonce-un-accord-sur-le-groenland-a-davos-et-suspend-ses-menaces-de-droits-de-douane_6663581_3210.html))*
- **Prime Minister Lecornu survives budget crisis using Article 49.3, announces housing plan after censure votes fail** — PM Sébastien Lecornu broke his promise and used Article 49.3 to pass the 2026 budget after parliamentary negotiations stalled. Two censure motions from LFI and RN were rejected, allowing him to announce a plan to build 2 million homes by 2030. *([lemonde.fr](https://lemonde.fr/politique/article/2026/01/20/budget-2026-sebastien-lecornu-engage-la-responsabilite-de-son-gouvernement-sur-la-partie-recettes-premier-49-3-d-une-serie-de-trois_6663387_823448.html))*
- **Marine Le Pen testifies in crucial appeal trial, changes strategy as 2027 presidential candidacy hangs in balance** — Le Pen spent over 10 hours testifying in her appeal trial for alleged EU funds embezzlement, adopting a more conciliatory tone and admitting some 'negligence' while denying intentional wrongdoing. A magistrate revealed being approached by US emissaries about the case. *([lemonde.fr](https://lemonde.fr/societe/article/2026/01/21/proces-des-assistants-du-fn-marine-le-pen-livre-un-argumentaire-bien-rode-au-premier-jour-de-son-interrogatoire_6663424_3224.html))*
- **Jordan Bardella spotted with Italian princess, campaigns for RN municipal victories while distancing from Trump** — RN president Bardella was filmed leaving a Paris event with Maria Carolina de Bourbon des Deux-Siciles, sparking media buzz about his private life. He campaigned for 'several dozens' of RN municipal victories while criticizing Trump's European policies. *([gala.fr](https://www.20minutes.fr/arts-stars/people/4197044-20260120-jordan-bardella-maria-carolina-bourbon-deux-siciles-princesse-vue-president-rn))*
- **France launches military service recruitment campaign and announces major defense exercises** — The Armed Forces Ministry launched recruitment for voluntary 10-month military service and announced the major 'Orion 26' exercise involving 12,500 troops. France also deployed forces to Greenland for Arctic Endurance exercises. *([actu.fr](https://lefigaro.fr/actualite-france/c-est-une-bonne-nouvelle-dans-la-creuse-le-nouveau-service-militaire-volontaire-redonne-espoir-a-tout-un-village-20260124))*
- **Macron announces social media ban for under-15s, accelerated legislative process planned** — President Macron announced plans to ban social media access for children under 15, with legislation to be in place by September 2026. The move follows similar initiatives in other countries and growing concerns about smartphone addiction among teenagers. *([euronews.com](https://euronews.com/2026/01/25/macron-calls-for-ban-on-social-media-for-under-15s-to-be-in-place-by-september))*
- **France prepares high-intensity warfare medical capabilities drawing lessons from Ukraine** — The Armed Forces Health Service is adapting to high-intensity conflict scenarios, learning from Ukraine war experiences with tourniquets, amputations, and drone-inflicted wounds. New training protocols are being implemented for potential major conflict scenarios. *([lefigaro.fr](https://lefigaro.fr/international/medecine-de-guerre-les-armees-reapprennent-a-soigner-en-haute-intensite-20260125))*
</Accordion>


